  - question: How do I know if my fascia is rotted?
    answer: "<p>Warning signs: paint peeling or bubbling, wood feels soft when you press (poke it with a screwdriver - if it sinks in easily, that's rot), dark staining, gutters pulling away from house, visible gaps between fascia and roof edge. We check fascia on every gutter estimate at no extra charge.</p>"
  - question: What causes fascia to rot?
    answer: "<p>Overflowing or leaking gutters, 90% of the time. Water runs behind the gutter, soaks into the fascia, never fully dries in Alabama humidity. Takes 3-5 years of consistent moisture to start visible rot. By the time you see it, it's been going on a while.</p>"
